"This Android phone's software gives Tether no call audio (the call sounds like silence to it). Calls are still answered, placed and ended here, but you hear and speak on the Android phone. A system update, or a self-test during a call that hears the call, turns call audio back on. If calls on the phone itself have no sound either, restart the phone once." = "NARM-AFZAR-E IN GOOSHI-E ANDROID BE REGISTER SEDAYE TAMAS NEMIDE. TAMASHA HANOOZ INJA JAVAB DADE, GEREFTE VA GHAT MISHAN, AMMA ROOYE GOOSHI-E ANDROID MISHNAVID VA HARF MIZANID. YE UPDATE-E SYSTEM, YA YE SELF-TEST VASAT-E TAMAS KE SEDA RO BESHNAVE, SEDAYE TAMAS RO DOBARE ROSHAN MIKONE. AGE TAMASHAYE KHOD-E GOOSHI HAM SEDA NADARAN, GOOSHI RO RESTART KONID.";
"Tether may not use this iPhone's microphone, so the other side hears nothing. Allow it in Settings › Privacy & Security › Microphone." = "REGISTER EJAZE-E ESTEFADE AZ MICROPHONE-E IN IPHONE RO NADARE, BARAYE HAMIN TARAF-E MOGHABEL CHIZI NEMISHNAVE. DAR SETTINGS › PRIVACY & SECURITY › MICROPHONE EJAZE BEDID.";
"Off is safest: on some Android phones muting their microphone also mutes your voice for the other side. When it is on, Tether checks during each call and turns the mute off if your voice does not get through." = "KHAMOOSH AMNTARE: ROOYE BAZI GOOSHIHAYE ANDROID BI-SEDA KARDAN-E MICROPHONESHOON SEDAYE SHOMA RO HAM BARAYE TARAF-E MOGHABEL GHAT MIKONE. VAGHTI ROSHANE, REGISTER DAR HAR TAMAS CHECK MIKONE VA AGE SEDAYE SHOMA NARESE, BI-SEDA RO KHAMOOSH MIKONE.";
