"Tether puts the call in Android's redirect audio mode: the Android phone's own microphone and earpiece leave the call, so the other side hears only this iPhone. Tether checks that both directions still work and keeps the microphone on where the phone does not allow it." = "REGISTER TAMAS RO BE HALAT-E \"REDIRECT\"-E ANDROID MIBARE: MICROPHONE VA GOOSHI-E KHOD-E ANDROID AZ TAMAS KHAREJ MISHAN, PAS TARAF-E MOGHABEL FAGHAT IN IPHONE RO MISHNAVE. REGISTER CHECK MIKONE HAR DO TARAF KAR KONAN VA JAYI KE GOOSHI EJAZE NADE MICROPHONE RO ROSHAN NEGAH MIDARE.";
